<Legal lang="en" seite="datenschutz" title="Privacy" kicker="Privacy" h1={`Privacy statement`} sub="Which data we process, for what, how long, and what rights you have.">
<section>
<h2>1 · Controller</h2>
<p>Responsible for the processing of personal data on im-stah.ch is:</p>
<dl class="def">
<div><dt>Company</dt><dd>Fernand Cina SA</dd></div>
<div><dt>Address</dt><dd>Bahnhofstrasse 27, 3970 Salgesch</dd></div>
<div><dt>E-mail</dt><dd>administration@fernand-cina.ch</dd></div>
<div><dt>Phone</dt><dd>027 455 09 08</dd></div>
</dl>
<p>Swiss data protection law applies. For people in the EU, the General Data Protection Regulation applies in addition.</p>
</section>

<section>
<h2>2 · Which data we process</h2>
<h3>2.1 Booking</h3>
<ul>
<li>Name of the person booking</li>
<li>E-mail address</li>
<li>Phone number, optional</li>
<li>Number of people</li>
<li>Name and food choice per person</li>
<li>Allergies, where reported</li>
<li>Payment data, processed by the payment provider</li>
</ul>
<h3>2.2 When visiting the website</h3>
<p>The server records technical data transmitted by the browser. This includes IP address, date, time, page called and browser type. This data serves operation and security.</p>
</section>

<section>
<h2>3 · What we process it for</h2>
<ul>
<li>Carrying out the booking and the event</li>
<li>Confirmation, reminder and questions</li>
<li>Buying and preparation by the kitchen, as figures per version</li>
<li>Billing and accounting</li>
<li>Sending news, where consented to</li>
</ul>
<p>Processing rests on the performance of the contract, on legal obligations and on an overriding interest in orderly operation.</p>
</section>

<section>
<h2>4 · Newsletter</h2>
<p>News is sent only with explicit consent. The corresponding box in the booking form is never pre-ticked.</p>
<p>We record the time, the source and the content of the consent. Revocation is possible at any time, through the unsubscribe link or by e-mail.</p>
<p>The basis is art. 3 para. 1 let. o of the Federal Act against Unfair Competition.</p>
</section>

<section>
<h2>5 · Disclosure</h2>
<p>We pass on personal data only as far as the event requires:</p>
<ul>
<li>Kitchen: number per version and reported allergies, without contact data</li>
<li>Payment provider: data to settle the payment</li>
<li>Hosting and booking system: technical storage on our behalf</li>
<li>Authorities: as far as required by law</li>
</ul>
<p>No sale of personal data takes place.</p>
</section>

<section>
<h2>6 · Retention</h2>
<p>We keep booking data until twelve months after the event. Accounting data we keep for ten years, as the law requires.</p>
<p>Data on newsletter consent we keep until revocation, then as evidence to a limited extent.</p>
</section>

<section>
<h2>7 · Your rights</h2>
<ul>
<li>Access to the data processed</li>
<li>Correction of inaccurate data</li>
<li>Deletion, where no retention obligation stands</li>
<li>Handover in a common format</li>
<li>Objection to a processing</li>
<li>Revocation of a consent given</li>
</ul>
<p>Write to administration@fernand-cina.ch. We handle the request within 30 days.</p>
<p>The competent supervisory authority is the Federal Data Protection and Information Commissioner in Bern.</p>
</section>

<section>
<h2>8 · Cookies and third-party services</h2>
<p>The website sets only technically necessary cookies. No analysis of behaviour by third parties takes place.</p>
<p>Maps and timetables are included as links, not embedded. Only on a click does the provider’s page open, and only then does it receive data.</p>
</section>

<section>
<h2>9 · Security</h2>
<p>Transmission is encrypted. We take appropriate technical and organisational measures to protect the data.</p>
<p>Complete security in transmission over the internet cannot be guaranteed by anyone.</p>
</section>

<section>
<h2>10 · Changes</h2>
<p>This statement may be adapted. The version published on im-stah.ch applies.</p>
</section>
</Legal>
